{"step_index":594,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:29:40Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:29:40+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:29:40+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/Challenge_e20263a9.lean`\nTotal Lines: 22\nTotal Bytes: 634\nShowing lines 1 to 22\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import Mathlib\n2: import LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n3: \n4: set_option maxRecDepth 10000\n5: \n6: open SimpleGraph\n7: \n8: -- Conjecture under test: (nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number\n9: -- Both declarations refer to the same `Candidate`.\n10: abbrev Candidate : Prop :=\n11:     ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n12:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\n13:       GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasRadius G → GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G\n14: \n15: lemma test_helper : 1 + 1 = 2 := rfl\n16: \n17: theorem prove_e20263a9 : Candidate := by\n18:   sorry\n19: \n20: theorem refute_e20263a9 : ¬ Candidate := by\n21:   sorry\n22: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
